# WHAT ENTERS (all three already committed to `src/` on fix/retirement; see their landing commits):
#   - CR1 (codegen): a RECURSIVE member of a bare inline union `A | B | …` is boxed, so a union whose
#     own member refers back to the union (the `Pattern`/`Type`-shaped retirements) has a finite,
#     correct C layout. `cg_union_field_inline_tag`.
#   - CR2 (checker + codegen): the inline-union GENERIC-INSTANCE mangle is STRUCTURE-ENCODED in BOTH
#     the checker (`variant_mangle`) and codegen (`cg_union_texpr_inst_mangle`), null-normalized so the
#     two agree — fixing the latent mangle-collision that blocked generic-over-inline-union widening.
#   - CR3 (parser + checker + codegen): the Family-A syntactic macro expander and `parse_pattern_primary`
#     accept an `@Type()` type-macro standing in a group-bind pattern position (`(@ns::Union()) as v`).
#     A new `MacroPattern` node holds the parsed `@name(...)`; `walk_pattern`/`walk_group_options` expand
#     it BEFORE type-check, re-parsing the macro's `lowering` fragment as a union `A | B | …` and splicing
#     each member in as a bare `BindPattern` option, so a `MacroPattern` never reaches the checker/codegen.
#     This is what lets a whole-union bind `X as v` survive the retirement of `type X = variant …` to `@X()`.
#   Carried forward from the prior reseeds: §14 A0-A4 / B1-B5 (the `@Type()` type-position expander over
#   every type position, incl. match-arm patterns; comptime reflection), §14 Form 2 parametric type-macros
#   (PT1 optional `: <type>` / `= <default>` params, PT2 comptime `if`-select over a bool param), §9.D
#   capabilities (a)/(b)/(c), the checker self-qualification fix, and the §9.D sweep so far (the 15 unions
#   retired before this reseed: FSpecKind, MergeDisposition, ConstValueKind, RegAssignment, BorrowedFrom,
#   ResidenceTier, RegexNode, Unique, PointsTo, ItemKind, LOp, MInst, MInstX86, File, TFSpecKind).
#
# CR3 IS INERT. No `src/` `.tks` writes an `@Type()` in a pattern position yet (the §9.D root retirements
